{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Torsion.neutron_proton_splitting","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Torsion.neutron_proton_splitting","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.neutron_proton_splitting_unconstrained_false","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.neutron_proton_splitting_unconstrained_false","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L132-L144","doc":"**The exact-equality form is refutable as written** — the base class\nnever relates the fields the conclusion names, so `∀ instances` admits\nones that simply disagree (and per §7ab the manuscript never claimed\nexact equality of the measured splitting to the derived value in the\nfirst place).  Kept as the documented evidence for why the resolving\ntheorem above states the prediction + tolerance form instead\n(bean qou-octr, criterion §10 `proof-unclosable-context-sorry`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.neutron_proton_splitting","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.neutron_proton_splitting","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L101-L130","doc":"**Neutron-proton mass splitting** ([`prop:neutron-proton-splitting`]),\nconditional on the corpus-pinned numerics — now **sorry-free**.\n\nThe framework *prediction* is `α · |Φ(udd) − Φ(uud)|`\n(`predictedNeutronProtonSplitting`); with the pinned values it equals\n`3.7449 · 0.3476 ≈ 1.3017 MeV` and agrees with the CODATA splitting\n`1.293 MeV` within the 1 % manuscript tolerance (measured error\n0.68 %).\n\nThe earlier flat form carried an *exact-equality* conjunct\n`m_n − m_p = α·|Φ(udd) − Φ(uud)|`, which over-claimed on two counts:\nit was refutable as written (`neutron_proton_splitting_unconstrained_false`\nbelow), and exact `=` between a measured mass difference and a derived\nvalue violates the §7ab approximation convention — the manuscript\nclaims `≈` with a stated tolerance, which is exactly conjunct (2)\nhere.  The prediction-formula conjunct (1) holds definitionally. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:neutron-proton-splitting","label":"prop:neutron-proton-splitting","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/neutron-proton-splitting.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingNumerics.Φ_udd_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingNumerics.Φ_udd_val","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L99-L99","doc":"Neutron (udd) traced-volume pin (provenance above). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingNumerics.Φ_uud_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingNumerics.Φ_uud_val","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L97-L97","doc":"Proton (uud) traced-volume pin (provenance above). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingNumerics.α_val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingNumerics.α_val","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L95-L95","doc":"Binding-scale pin `α = m_e·8G ≈ 3.7449` (provenance above). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingNumerics.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingNumerics.mk","kind":"ctor","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L93-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingNumerics.toNeutronProtonSplittingContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingNumerics.toNeutronProtonSplittingContext","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L93-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingNumerics","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingNumerics","kind":"class","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L76-L99","doc":"**Corpus-pinned numerics** for the splitting (the `qou-octr` fix: give\nthe class the hypotheses the derivation needs).  Each pin is a genuine\n*input* with provenance, not the conclusion:\n\n- `α = 3.7449` — the binding scale `m_e·8G` (`m_e = 0.511 MeV`,\n  `G` Catalan's constant, `8G ≈ 7.3286`); same scale as the atomic\n  mass formula.\n- `Φ(uud) = −0.8785`, `Φ(udd) = −1.2261` — the canonical Hecke\n  traced-volumes of the quark orderings; **derived** in the corpus\n  with exact closed forms (`log` of a rational function of `q`), see\n  `docs/audits/2026-07-11-quark-volume-provenance.md` and\n  `computations/level1-qvalues.py`.  Decimal pins at manuscript\n  precision (4 d.p.); porting the closed forms themselves to Lean is\n  the remaining formalization item.\n\nFrom these three pins the CODATA agreement below is *derived* by\narithmetic — the class does not carry the conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.predictedNeutronProtonSplitting","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.predictedNeutronProtonSplitting","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L71-L74","doc":"The framework-predicted neutron-proton mass difference in MeV\n(`α · |Φ(udd) − Φ(uud)|` per the manuscript). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingContext.m_n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingContext.m_n","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Neutron rest mass (MeV). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingContext.m_p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingContext.m_p","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Proton rest mass (MeV). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingContext.Φ_udd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingContext.Φ_udd","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Quantum-dilogarithm volume of the neutron (udd) braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingContext.Φ_uud","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingContext.Φ_uud","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L63-L63","doc":"Quantum-dilogarithm volume of the proton (uud) braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingContext.α","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingContext.α","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Binding scale `α = m_e · 8G`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.NeutronProtonSplittingContext","kind":"class","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L56-L69","doc":"Inputs for the neutron-proton splitting: the binding scale `α = m_e·8G`,\nthe proton/neutron quantum-dilogarithm volumes `Φ(uud)`, `Φ(udd)`, and\nthe physical masses `m_p`, `m_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.codataNeutronProtonSplittingMeV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.codataNeutronProtonSplittingMeV","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/neutron_proton_splitting.lean#L51-L54","doc":"The CODATA-derived neutron-proton mass difference in MeV (CODATA 2022:\n`939.56542194 − 938.27208816 = 1.29333378 MeV`; manuscript rounds to\n`1.293`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}